{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Root cause (investigated, not yet fixed)\n\n`.github/workflows/verify-identity.yml:36-39` checks out with `filter: blob:none` and\n`fetch-depth: 0` but **no `ref:`**. `actions/checkout` therefore fetches *all branch heads* —\nincluding the `tickets` branch — before the pack budget is measured at lines 41-58 and judged at\nlines 114-116. The budget is judging an all-refs object database, not a main-only code checkout.\n\nRun 35480996877's log confirms the fetch shape:\n`git fetch --no-tags --prune --no-recurse-submodules --filter=blob:none origin\n+refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/* +refs/tags/*:refs/tags/*`.\n\n### Measured reproduction\n\nScratch clones against the same remote, same `--filter=blob:none`:\n\n| checkout shape | `git count-objects -vH` |\n|---|---:|\n| main-only blobless fetch, checkout `origin/main` | `size-pack: 22.84 MiB`, in-pack 30519 |\n| all-heads blobless fetch, checkout `origin/main` | `size-pack: 633.02 MiB`, in-pack 820686 |\n| the failing CI run | `648484 KiB` = ~633.29 MiB |\n\nThe all-heads shape reproduces CI to within ~0.27 MiB. That is the root cause, confirmed\nempirically rather than inferred.\n\nA single large blob is ruled out as the direct cause: this pack is *blobless*. `origin/tickets`\nreachable under `--filter=blob:none` is dominated by non-blob history — 496160 tree objects and\n293827 commits, zero blobs. The volume is tickets-branch tree/commit history pulled in because\n`tickets` was fetched as part of all heads.\n\n### Why the previous fix did not prevent this\n\n`e900fa14ad5` (\"Stop pack budget pre-empting authorship gate\") only split the gate into a\nmeasure half and a judge half so the budget verdict stops pre-empting the authorship verdict. It\ndeliberately left the limit, the checkout shape, and the fail-closed behaviour unchanged, so it\ncannot reduce the measured pack.\n\n### The in-repo working example\n\nOther workflows that need full history already scope the checkout to main:\n`reconcile-bridge-canary.yml:88-98` and `dependency-advisory-canary.yml:64-72` both set\n`filter: blob:none`, `fetch-depth: 0` **and `ref: main`**. `verify-identity.yml` is the outlier.\n\n### Proposed fix — narrow the checkout, do NOT raise the budget\n\nAdd `ref: main` to the initial `actions/checkout`. The later explicit\n`git fetch origin '+tickets:refs/remotes/origin/tickets'` still mounts the tickets store for\nidentity verification, and it runs *after* the measurement.\n\nThis is the right shape of fix: the 563200 KiB limit is already a temporary bridge (the deliberate\nbudget is 102400 KiB per `fluorspar-comparable-zeren`, raised while 536b history reclaim lands),\nand ADR 0106 establishes the budget as an intentional growth canary. Raising it again would\nsilence the canary; narrowing the checkout removes the reason to.\n\nAdds no new gate, env var, config key, feature flag, lock, fixture or helper, so it should not\ntrip the mechanism-delta, module-size, or complexity ratchets."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789884778846908276,"uuid":"e86c41b7-6b15-4ccf-bce0-92f839afa06a"}